.TH KULAN-SETTINGS 1 "October 2026" "Kulan OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kulan-settings \- Kulan OS settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kulan-settings
[\fIpage\fR] [\fB\-\-check\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kulan-settings
is one place for Kulan OS options: appearance, the dock, the top bar,
desktop and windows, Night Light and display, keyboard, login items,
updates and recovery, add-ons and About Kulan OS. Pages that belong to GNOME
Settings (Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, sound, displays, users) are listed too and open
there.
.PP
Installing updates or add-ons and changing automatic updates ask for an
administrator password through
.BR pkexec (1).
.SH PAGES
.IR appearance ", " dock ", " top-bar ", " desktop ", " display ", "
.IR keyboard ", " login-items ", " updates ", " add-ons ", " about .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Open Software Update and check for new updates.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
Build every page, then quit; exits non-zero if a page fails. Used by
automated tests.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/kulan/addons.json
The add-ons offered on the Add-ons page.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kulan/updates.ini
The "Create a restore point before installing" choice.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gtk-4.0/gtk.css, ~/.config/gtk-3.0/gtk.css
Where the Kulan window-button style is switched on or off.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gnome-control-center (1),
.BR timeshift (1)
